# UBSan errors the tests let pass, each a finding of the host tests left as
# it is on the iPod; the firmware's build is not changed by the tests.
#
# itunesdb.c: metadata_room() puts the records' pool right after a table of
# 32-bit offsets, so with an odd number of songs every struct meta_record,
# which starts with a uint64_t, is 4 bytes off 8. The PP5022's ARMv4 reads a
# 64-bit value as two words, which need only 4: right on the iPod, wrong on a
# CPU with LDRD's alignment. Shown by the case odd-tracks.
alignment:cmp_meta
